      <guid>https://rmoff.net/cuttings/2026/10/16/from-data-contracts-to-quality-checks/</guid>
      <description>&lt;article class=&#34;cutting cutting-shared&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;div class=&#34;cutting-meta&#34; data-pagefind-ignore&gt; &lt;time class=&#34;cutting-date&#34; datetime=&#34;2026-10-16&#34;&gt;16 Oct 2026&lt;/time&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;div class=&#34;cutting-card&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;h2 class=&#34;cutting-title&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://gambilldataengineering.substack.com/p/from-data-contracts-to-quality-checks&#34;&gt;From Data Contracts to Quality Checks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;p class=&#34;cutting-source&#34;&gt;Chris Gambill · gambilldataengineering.substack.com&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;figure class=&#34;cutting-quote&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;blockquote cite=&#34;https://gambilldataengineering.substack.com/p/from-data-contracts-to-quality-checks&#34;&gt;&lt;p&gt;A data contract only earns its keep when its computable requirements become enforceable checks.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Scattering assertions throughout notebooks does not solve that problem. Neither does documenting requirements in a wiki that has no connection to runtime behavior.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/article&gt;&#xA;</description>
